<title>SPAIN: SOCCER-ROMA CHASING SEVILLA'S ALMEYDA.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-ROMA CHASING SEVILLA'S ALMEYDA.</headline>
<dateline>SEVILLE, Spain 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Struggling Sevilla are negotiating the transfer of Argentine midfielder Matias Almeyda to Roma.</p>
<p>&quot;We need liquidity to close the year's accounts,&quot; said Herminio Menendez, director general of the financially-troubled club, who are currently bottom of the Spanish first division.</p>
<p>Sevilla paid River Plate a club record $10 million for the player earlier in the season.</p>
<p>Roma are understood to have offered $6 million for Almeyda but the Spanish side want at least $1 million more.</p>
</text>
